@startuml
title NestJS Routes — regressão de criação e eventos com mocks (v1.1.0 proposta)
actor "Jest" as Test
participant "RoutesService" as Routes
participant "DirectionsService (mock)" as Maps
database "Prisma route (mock)" as Prisma
queue "Kafka Producer (mock)" as Kafka
participant "RoutesDriverService" as Driver
database "Prisma routeDriver (mock)" as RouteDriver
participant "WebSocket gateway (mock)" as Gateway
Test -> Routes : create({source_id,destination_id,name})
Routes -> Maps : getDirections(place_id,...)
Maps --> Routes : legs, steps, distance, duration
Routes -> Prisma : route.create(...directions)
Prisma --> Routes : route id
Routes -> Kafka : send(RouteCreated, points)
Routes --> Test : route persistida
Test -> Routes : startRoute(id)
Routes -> Prisma : findUniqueOrThrow
alt rota ausente
 Prisma --> Routes : rejeita
 Routes --> Test : erro, sem evento Kafka
else rota existente
 Prisma --> Routes : rota
 Routes -> Kafka : send(DeliveryStarted)
end
Test -> Driver : processRoute({route_id,lat,lng})
Driver -> RouteDriver : upsert(point)
RouteDriver --> Driver : registro
Driver -> Gateway : emitNewPoints(payload)
Gateway --> Test : canal individual + global (mesmo ponto)
Test -> Gateway : handleMessage() com rota simulada
Gateway --> Test : broadcasts do início e fim (lat,lng corretos)
note bottom
Quatro suites de lógica isolada. O CI não sobe
MongoDB/Kafka/Google Maps nem valida outbox.
end note
@enduml
